Specification: slugify accepts a string and returns a lowercase slug: every MAXIMAL run of non-alphanumeric characters is replaced by a single hyphen, all letters are lowercased, and leading and trailing hyphens are stripped. The result may be an empty string.

```python
def slugify(text):
    out = []
    for ch in text.lower():
        if ch.isalnum():
            out.append(ch)
        else:
            out.append('-')
    return ''.join(out)
